From 203a13a0e5fce93d105dfe5e05741ba6291240c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 17 May 2026 06:32:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(thm-verify): step-level anchor refresh + analyzer for
 Theorem 1 (App. F)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

App. F empirical verification of Theorem 1 (Anchor Stability). The
TADS paper §4.5 declared the measurement but had no instrumentation,
no analysis pipeline, and no pass/fail gates. This change adds all of
that without changing the theorem statement or the regular training path.

- TrajectoryAnchor: optional track_sigma flag keeps the previous Σ per
  layer so update() can report ‖Σ^(t+1) − Σ^(t)‖_F (assumption A1).
  Also exposes d_step (= ‖v^(t+1) − v^(t)‖), sign_inner_prev, and a
  flat last_measurement dict for the verifier to drain. Restores the
  model's train/eval mode on exit so step-level refresh inside the SFT
  loop doesn't silently leave the model in eval mode.

- TheoremVerifier: rank-0 owner of the JSONL writer and the FIXED probe
  Subset (same indices across all refresh points so Σ drift reflects
  only model drift). Fires every N optimizer steps; dumps per-(step,
  layer) rows + per-step anchor vectors (.npy) for the offline cumulative
  bound (conclusion C2). No-op when disabled, so existing configs are
  untouched.

- sft.sft_one_epoch: one hook line at each optimizer.step() boundary
  forwards (model, lr, epoch) to the verifier. The verifier owns its
  own cumulative-optstep counter so the caller stays bookkeeping-free.

- train.py: builds the verifier when cfg.verification.enabled and
  method == "tads"; passes it through to sft_one_epoch.

- thm_verify_05b config: drop-in extension of light_tads_05b that turns
  on verification with refresh_every_optstep=50 → ≈39 measurement points
  over 3 epochs on a single GPU.

- analyze_theorem.py: offline analyser. Runs E2 first (linear regression
  ΔΣ_F vs lr → C_Σ), then uses that C_Σ to compute the per-step bound
  for E3. Generates F1–F4 (PNG + PDF for LaTeX), table_F1 (CSV + TeX),
  and summary.json / PASS_FAIL.json so the App. F numbers and §4.5
  paragraph can be drafted directly from machine-readable output.

- tests/test_theorem_verification.py: smoke covers (i) anchor track_sigma
  path produces finite ΔΣ_F and d_step from t≥1, (ii) train/eval mode
  preserved across update(), (iii) verifier cadence + JSONL + .npy
  outputs, (iv) disabled-verifier no-op, and (v) the analyzer end-to-end
  on a synthetic Theorem-satisfying signal where it recovers C_Σ to
  within 5 % and emits PASS for all five verdicts.

No real training run was attempted in this environment — that requires
the 0.5B model + alpaca-gpt4 + a GPU. Land this branch, run
  python -m tads.train --config configs/experiments/thm_verify_05b.yaml
on a node that has them, then
  python scripts/analyze_theorem.py --run_dir <run_dir>
